# payload-331.hex — Data loader for fx-570ES+/fx-991ES+ (GY454XE ROM)
# Provenance: Universal Casio Forum thread 7583 ("FX-82/-83GT/-115/-991ES PLUS Hacking"),
# page 9, post #331 by user202729, 2018-05-27 ("Data loader for 570ES+").
# Payload was compiled with user202729's compiler.py (github.com/user202729/fxesplus,
# 570esp/compiler.py) and is stated as "Tested on the emulator". Our ROM:
# models/fx570esplus/rom.bin, SHA-256 1a1b575f…71071 (GY454XE) — same image the
# compiler toolchain targets.
#
# The 100-byte payload is written to the COMP input buffer at 0x8154; the ROP
# chain takes over at the PC=0x2768 / SP=8DA4 execution point (see inject() in
# models/fx570esplus/model.lua). It then:
#   1. getkeycode() twice — byte value = k1 + k2 (sum of two hardware keycodes)
#   2. writes that byte to (*y), y starting at 0xF830 (framebuffer row 3, col 0)
#   3. increments y by 1 (next byte goes one address up, filling rows 3..)
#   4. restores the stack (strcpy self-copy) and loops forever (home: goto start)
# There is no way to break the loop except overwriting the loop itself.
#
# Effect: every two key presses append one fully controlled byte to the
# framebuffer → arbitrary custom output on the 96x32 display, via ROP.
#
# 200 hex digits / 100 bytes:
3130e23d3030a032303030f86a273030b244303001012c8531306c743030868b0a44303033333333ee543130b38b4f8b602730306a4f3030268c684f30303334353637383930313260b430308c46313060b43030e23d3030b02c30303333631e3130ec6c
